Description: The Vulkan stereo layer gives an X11 window its pair where the X server has no DRI3
 On an X server without DRI3 (Xwayland without glamor: no 3D acceleration,
 or XWAYLAND_NO_GLAMOR=1) the layer refused a swapchain of two image layers
 with VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT after raising maxImageArrayLayers to 2,
 so a program that asked for stereo ended and nobody was told; lavapipe's
 own X11 presentation returned VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR at its first present.
 .
 Measured on NVIDIA's driver without DRI3: its presentation puts the whole
 swapchain image into the window with one core PutImage (no MIT-SHM, no
 Present, so no completion), accepts an extent other than the window's, and
 returns VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR at the first present after the window's
 size changed. lavapipe without DRI3 uses Mesa's PutImage path, which
 compares the extent with the window. In both a picture of both views is
 whole only in a window two views wide.
 .
 Stereo KWin makes a top-level window it manages, declared full side by side
 without _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_VERSION 4 (version 3, the default), twice
 as wide and sends the program a synthetic ConfigureNotify of one view. So
 on such a server the window is declared that way, and the swapchain of both
 views is made once the X server reports the window two views wide (at most
 MESA_STEREO_DOUBLING_WAIT_MS, 1000 by default, while the window is mapped;
 the gl-stereo layer waits the same way): "With Xcb, minImageExtent,
 maxImageExtent, and currentExtent must always equal the window size"
 (VK_KHR_xcb_surface). The program keeps working in one view's size, the
 surface's extent halved while the window is two views wide. A doubling
 that comes later makes the driver's swapchain out of date, as any resize of
 an X11 window does. A swapchain of one view after a pair withdraws the
 declaration and is made once the window is one view wide again.
 .
 A child window or an override-redirect one is not made wider by the
 compositor, nor is any window by a compositor that announces less than
 version 3. There the layer offers one image layer, and a program that asks
 for two anyway is refused and the person is told through
 sparky-stereo-problems (package mesa-vulkan-layer-stereo, key
 one-view:vulkan:DEVICE, message LOCAL4 with the program, the device and
 Mesa's own words); a pair of that device shown later ends it. The problem
 transport takes up to four message arguments for this.
 .
 On a server with DRI3 nothing changes.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed, the stereo declaration and the Vulkan stereo layer are the edition's own
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Last-Update: 2026-11-16

